{
  "_comment": [
    "Farm buildings and home upgrades.",
    "",
    "WHY HAND-AUTHORED. The Coop, Barn and Farmhouse tables are rowspan grids —",
    "one requirement cell spans four rows, one capacity cell spans two — and the",
    "columns differ on all three pages. Reading them by index means tracking which",
    "column a spanned cell belongs to, which is the fragile half of table parsing.",
    "Eleven records, read once.",
    "",
    "COLOURS ARE NOT TIERS. The Carpenter sells a Red and a White blueprint for",
    "every coop and barn at the same price, capacity and requirement. They are one",
    "building each, not two — the colour is cosmetic and belongs to the shop's",
    "stock list, where both blueprints already appear.",
    "",
    "SOURCES. Coop and Barn tiers from their own pages' Blueprints tables;",
    "greenhouse prices from the Carpenter's Buildings table and its MATERIALS",
    "from the Greenhouse page's own table — the Carpenter's states none, which",
    "is why both tiers shipped material-less for a release; home upgrades from",
    "Farmhouse (transcluded onto the Carpenter page as 'Home Upgrade'). Checked",
    "2026-08-07; every building re-verified against its own page 2026-08-19",
    "(coop, barn and farmhouse matched exactly — only the greenhouse gained).",
    "",
    "GREENHOUSE CAPACITY is growing space (5x5 and 10x10 tiles), not animals, so",
    "`capacity` is null rather than 25 and 100 — the field means occupants",
    "everywhere else and a number that means something different in one record is",
    "worse than an absent one.",
    "",
    "BLUEPRINTS are the tier's purchasable items, named by display name and",
    "resolved through the build's id index like materials. The two names per",
    "tier are the colour variants the comment above describes — a set of",
    "equivalent choices, not two buildings. Verified against the carpenter's",
    "shipped stock 2026-08-18; note the White coop/barn blueprints' internal",
    "ids say 'black', which is why this file speaks display names.",
    "",
    "KITCHEN tiers are the three kitchen types on the Carpenter page (checked",
    "2026-08-18): Beginner 1000t ungated, Cozy 1500t at Cooking 15, Adept 3000t",
    "at Cooking 30. No materials stated. Only the Beginner exists as an item",
    "(beginner_kitchen), so only tier 1 carries a blueprint-style item link.",
    "CRAFTING STATION is a single 1000t tier, ungated — stated identically on",
    "the Crafting and Carpenter pages. FARM EXPANSION is one 40000t expansion",
    "with 50 Refined Stone + 50 Hard Wood, no stated prerequisite (Farm page,",
    "same date). THE MILL is not bought at all: repair_quest names the",
    "game-derived quest whose supplied items are the whole cost, so its tiers",
    "stay empty deliberately — a tesserae figure there would be invented."
  ],

